:431,"570":142,"571":153,"572":125,"573":118,"574":143,"575":132,"576":144,"577":29,"578":51,"579":59,"580":38,"581":285,"582":571,"583":543,"584":162,"585":158,"586":161,"587":159,"588":527,"589":210,"590":163,"591":164,"592":160,"593":330,"594":479,"595":584,"596":496,"597":364,"598":378,"599":394,"600":154,"601":151,"602":146,"603":149,"604":152,"605":453,"606":395,"607":52,"608":57,"609":49,"610":44,"611":649,"612":578,"613":533,"614":567,"615":209,"616":416,"617":560,"618":473,"619":436,"620":388,"621":558,"622":537,"623":572,"624":216,"625":243,"626":245,"627":219,"628":434,"629":396,"630":176,"631":189,"632":171,"633":166,"634":184,"635":117,"636":48,"637":17,"638":80,"639":71,"640":112,"641":36,"642":34,"643":97,"644":47,"645":576,"646":475,"647":579,"648":391,"649":658,"650":408,"651":455,"652":409,"653":653,"654":401,"655":234,"656":428,"657":392,"658":462,"659":242,"660":519,"661":534,"662":485},"orderedDocs":[[359,"\"Can you prep a mutual action plan for this deal?\" She engages Oliv AI's MAP Manager agent."],[357,"\"Draft the follow-up from my call this afternoon.\" Olivia pulls from the meeting transcript and drafts it."],[360,"\"I just met six people at an event, line up outreach for each of them.\" She engages Oliv AI's Prospector agent."],[358,"\"This deal has been stuck for three weeks.\" She engages Oliv AI's Re-Activator agent and surfaces a re-engagement strategy."],[207,"**1:1s start at strategy.** Rep reviews arrive prepped, so the meeting skips twenty minutes of status updates."],[501,"**A brief built around the deal.** Oliv AI's brief shows qualification status against your methodology and a recommended agenda. Avoma documents templates that standardize meeting prep by meeting purpose. Compare Oliv AI vs Avoma."],[253,"**A daily rhythm, not a weekly check.** Deal Driver sends a morning brief and a sunset summary every day. Gong's pipeline generation dashboard recipe says it should be viewed weekly. See Oliv AI as a Gong alternative."],[477,"**A follow-up email draft.** It covers what was discussed, what was agreed and the next steps, with dates where possible. You review, adjust and send. See how a strong sales follow-up converts."],[116,"**A middle setting between asking and acting.** With **Agent Decides**, the agent judges whether to ask before it uses a tool. Fireflies.ai documents choosing which permissions AskFred has in each connected app."],[502,"**A nudge, not a list to check.** Oliv AI nudges the rep directly when next steps go overdue. Gong's to-do filter lets you show to-dos that are due or overdue. See Oliv AI as a Gong alternative."],[504,"**Active opportunities only.** Meeting Assistant works on meetings linked to an active opportunity. Researcher covers first-time contacts."],[365,"**Add email, if you can.** Email is optional, but it adds a lot of context between meetings. LinkedIn or Sales Navigator is optional too, for contact enrichment."],[122,"**Add Tool is grayed out on some agents.** On the full-height tools layout used by the richer agent pages, the button is disabled, with no message saying why."],[220,"**Adjust the brief format if you want to.** Managers can customize alert sensitivity and brief format."],[232,"**After the meeting.** Once the recording is processed, the follow-up email is drafted, CRM field updates are proposed and qualification gaps are flagged, all within five minutes of the call ending."],[125,"**Agent Decides isn't explained in the product.** The menu offers it without saying what the agent weighs."],[114,"**Agents that act beyond their own app.** Oliv AI's tools update CRM records, send email and post to Slack. Gong's help center says its agents generate outputs within Gong Assistant and do not perform actions in external systems. See Oliv AI as a Gong alternative."],[637,"**An agenda built from the deal.** Oliv AI's recommended agenda follows the deal stage and the open qualification gaps. Avoma documents sharing an agenda that you build from a notes template. See Oliv AI vs Avoma."],[252,"**An alert with a next move.** Each Deal Driver alert carries the deal, the signal, the context and a suggested action. Avoma's Deal Health produces a 0 to 100 risk score with a Low, Medium or High classification. Compare Oliv AI vs Avoma."],[387,"**Answers that lead to action.** Olivia drafts the follow-up and surfaces CRM updates for review after a call. Avoma describes Global Ask Avoma as an assistant for asking questions about your organization's data. Compare Oliv AI vs Avoma."],[113,"**Approval set per action.** Oliv AI gives each tool its own run mode, so lookups and writes on one agent can differ. Outreach's Omni pauses for confirmation before any change to a Prospect, Account or Opportunity record."],[508,"**Auto mode comes later.** Updates stay in review until RevOps confirms the switch to auto mode."],[119,"**Auto Run is the default.** A tool that stores no mode shows **Auto Run**, and moving a tool to **Auto Run** asks for no confirmation. Check new tools before an agent goes live."],[128,"**Auto Run**, unless the tool stores a different mode. That means the agent acts without asking, so set writes to **Requires Approval** if you want a person to check them."],[231,"**Before the meeting.** About 30 minutes before every meeting on an active opportunity, the rep gets a deal summary, qualification status against the methodology, stakeholder context and a recommended agenda. MEDDPICC, BANT or a custom framework all work."],[459,"**Briefed before you join.** A one-screen brief lands about 30 minutes before each deal meeting."],[486,"**Buying committee roles.** It tracks each contact's role on the opportunity, such as economic buyer, champion or blocker."],[218,"**Confirm the team roster and manager hierarchy.** Deal Driver needs both to know whose deals roll up to whom."],[362,"**Connect a recording or transcript input.** Oliv Notetaker, or an equivalent, is the primary source of her live context."],[577,"**Connect three things.** The brief draws on your calendar, your call recording tool or Oliv AI's own recorder, and your CRM: Salesforce, HubSpot or Zoho."],[364,"**Connect your calendar.** It's how she knows which meetings are coming up."],[216,"**Connect your CRM.** Deal Driver reads Deal Insights data: stage, amount, close date and next steps."],[363,"**Connect your CRM.** It gives her pipeline and deal history. Oliv AI works as a layer on top of the CRM, alongside your other connected tools."],[217,"**Connect your team's calendar.** Meeting and activity data from Oliv feed the morning brief and the alerts."],[642,"**Connections come first.** No brief arrives until your calendar, recorder and CRM are connected. Most teams are connected within a week."],[391,"**Conversations aren't saved.** A conversation can't be named, reopened or searched, and leaving the screen loses it."],[641,"**Deal briefs need a deal.** The deal brief covers meetings linked to an active opportunity in your CRM. Meetings with new contacts get the research brief instead."],[471,"**Deal summary.** Stage, amount, close date, last activity and next steps."],[580,"**Don't wait for a clean CRM.** Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent fills in missing or stale fields from call history as it goes, so the brief works from day one."],[392,"**English only.** Olivia works in English."],[199,"**Event-triggered alerts.** A signal during the day when a deal stalls, a stage drifts or a high-value opportunity goes quiet."],[64,"**Every action sits in one list.** Each card names the action and says in a sentence what it does, so nothing an agent can do is hidden."],[500,"**Every core deal field, proposed after each call.** Oliv AI proposes stage, amount, close date, qualification fields and next steps from the conversation. Gong's deal boards fill one text-only CRM field with AI-suggested updates. Compare Oliv AI vs Gong."],[461,"**Fields proposed, not typed.** You accept, edit or reject each suggested CRM update."],[610,"**First calls get research too.** New contacts come with company and person context and an opening line."],[334,"**Follow-up drafted for you.** After a call, the follow-up email is drafted and ready within minutes."],[460,"**Follow-up written from the call.** The email draft comes from the actual transcript, not a template."],[644,"**Follow-ups are drafts.** The follow-up email and CRM updates wait for you to review before anything is sent or saved."],[636,"**Gaps inside the brief.** Oliv AI's brief shows qualification status against your methodology, next to the agenda. Gong documents a separate MEDDICC agent that shows where the gaps are. See Oliv AI as a Gong alternative."],[609,"**Gaps show up early.** Open qualification questions appear while you can still ask them."],[353,"**Get me ready for my [account] renewal call at 4pm today.**"],[578,"**Have the deal in your CRM.** Deal briefs cover meetings linked to an active opportunity. First meetings with new contacts get a research brief instead."],[607,"**It arrives without asking.** The brief lands 30 minutes before the meeting, with nothing to request."],[255,"**It doesn't update CRM fields.** Deal Driver surfaces data quality gaps. CRM Manager makes the updates."],[257,"**It isn't a coaching tool.** Coach handles rep development."],[256,"**It isn't the forecast.** Forecaster handles pipeline projection and accuracy. Deal Driver handles real-time visibility and alerts."],[505,"**It needs a recording.** Meeting Assistant relies on Oliv Notetaker recordings and transcripts and a Deal Insights subscription."],[608,"**It reads in a minute.** One screen, about 60 seconds, scannable on the way into the room."],[258,"**It's built for sales teams.** Customer success managers use Portfolio Manager instead."],[579,"**Know your methodology.** Qualification status is shown against the framework your company runs."],[366,"**Let Oliver set the playbook.** RevOps and leadership configure Oliver with your stages, ownership and handoffs, and Olivia operates inside those rules from day one."],[487,"**Meetings that weren't recorded.** It can prompt you for a quick voice summary and use that as a data source."],[203,"**Monday rollup.** A ready-to-review pipeline summary for leadership, prepared before the first standup."],[198,"**Morning brief.** Today's meetings across the team, flags for meetings where the manager's attendance or notes would help, and priority deals to watch, based on the prior 24 hours."],[483,"**New people and companies.** When a meeting, call or email involves a company or person not yet in the CRM, it creates the record and enriches it."],[124,"**No connection status.** The tab doesn't show whether a tool's system is connected."],[394,"**No dispatch log.** You see which agent did a piece of work through its \"Drafted by\" line, not through a list of hand-offs."],[120,"**No role check.** Anyone who can reach an agent's **Tools** tab can change a tool's mode."],[393,"**No warning on Act without asking.** Oliver shows a **High Risk** banner for this setting and Olivia doesn't, so check the dropdown before you leave a conversation."],[506,"**Not a CRM.** CRM Manager works on top of Salesforce, HubSpot or Zoho. It doesn't replace them."],[390,"**Not in the marketplace.** Browsing agents won't find Olivia. Reach her through the side panel, the chat page or an **Agent Feed** row."],[639,"**On the calendar, not on a trigger.** Oliv AI sends the brief 30 minutes before each meeting on an active opportunity. Gong's automated briefs go out when predefined CRM conditions are met. See Gong vs Oliv AI."],[336,"**One place to ask.** You tell Olivia what you need, and she routes it to the right agent."],[118,"**One tool at a time.** There's no bulk control, and no agent-wide or workspace-wide default mode."],[507,"**Pending updates have a deadline.** If a rep doesn't complete updates within a defined window, deals can be deferred or flagged as closed-lost. Each org configures this."],[201,"**Per-rep 1:1 reports.** Each rep's pipeline, activity, deal health and flagged items, delivered every Thursday before the manager's first meeting of the day."],[333,"**Prep that's already done.** She surfaces deal context about 30 minutes before a meeting, so you don't rebuild it yourself."],[478,"**Proposed deal field updates.** Stage, amount, close date, qualification fields and next steps, based on what was said."],[479,"**Qualification gap flags.** New information, or notable absences, that change the deal's qualification status."],[472,"**Qualification status.** Where the deal stands against your methodology, with gaps and open questions highlighted. MEDDPICC, BANT, SPICED, MEDPICS and custom frameworks are supported."],[638,"**Ready for people you've never met.** Oliv AI's first-meeting brief covers the company, the person and an icebreaker. Fireflies.ai builds its brief from your previous meetings with the same attendees."],[474,"**Recommended agenda.** Tailored to the deal stage and the qualification gaps."],[208,"**Reps get time back.** A follow-up is drafted in about five minutes for the rep to review and send."],[65,"**Risk is set where it lives.** A record lookup and a stage update on the same agent can run under different modes."],[335,"**Risk raised early.** She flags deals with no activity, close dates nearing without progress, or qualification gaps."],[206,"**Risk shows up early.** Alerts fire the moment deals stall or stages drift, not when a rep escalates."],[67,"**Routine reads stay quick.** **Auto Run** lets low-risk actions happen without a prompt."],[219,"**Set your alert thresholds.** Choose inactivity windows, field completion requirements and deal value thresholds, per manager or per team."],[395,"**She doesn't own process.** Stages, ownership and handoffs are set through Oliver."],[259,"**Signals depend on the data.** Deal Driver's signals are only as good as the data behind them, which is why CRM Manager matters."],[473,"**Stakeholders.** Who is in the meeting, what roles they play and what they care about, based on prior conversations."],[462,"**Stalls flagged early.** You get a nudge when next steps go overdue or activity drops."],[200,"**Sunset summary.** Deals won or lost that day, meetings that happened and their key outcomes, deals newly flagged at risk, and open situations to follow up."],[485,"**Tasks from next steps.** It creates tasks from the next steps in meetings, calls and emails, and assigns them to the right owner."],[202,"**Team pipeline review.** A rolled-up view of the team's pipeline health, coverage and risk profile, ready for leadership reviews."],[251,"**The 1:1 report comes to you.** Deal Driver compiles each rep's pipeline every Thursday and puts it in the manager's inbox. Gong recommends checking a deal board weekly, particularly before 1:1s and pipeline reviews. Compare Oliv AI vs Gong."],[205,"**The day starts briefed.** Meetings, risks and deals that need attention first are surfaced before the day starts."],[643,"**The research brief is short by design.** It's three bullets and an icebreaker. The full detail view is in the platform."],[484,"**The right deal.** It maps each activity to the right account and opportunity, including multi-threaded deals. If it can't resolve one, it asks you."],[121,"**Tools can't be removed or reordered.** There's no delete control on a tool card or in the sidebar."],[123,"**Tools have no settings of their own.** There are no parameters, field mappings or filters, so you can't limit a tool to certain records or fields."],[126,"**Two labels for one idea.** The dropdown says **Requires Approval**; the **Overview** heading says **Human-Reviewed**."],[352,"**What does my day look like?**"],[354,"**Where are my deals getting stuck the most?**"],[386,"**Work handed off, not just answered.** Olivia dispatches the right specialist agent for each task and reports back. Gong's help centre describes agents as personal assets that each team member creates for