iet with no activity, no CRM flag and no alert. A week later, the rep says \"it's progressing\" at the standup. By day fourteen the deal is cold and the rep escalates, after two or more weeks of invisible risk."],[223,"A deal enters a risk state, such as no activity for a set number of days or a close date approaching without progress."],[225,"A deal stage changes unexpectedly, moving backward or stalling mid-stage."],[615,"A first call is mostly won or lost in its opening minutes. The SDR doesn't need everything about the account, just the few facts that make the opening specific. That's a short job if someone else has already done the reading."],[589,"A first meeting has no deal history to draw on, so the prep is research. Tell Oliv AI's Olivia agent you're meeting someone for the first time and ask her to prepare you. Thirty minutes before the meeting, she sends three bullets and an icebreaker:"],[481,"A full history of how each field was updated stays visible. Once accuracy thresholds are met, RevOps can confirm the switch to auto mode."],[226,"A high-value opportunity goes quiet."],[405,"A recording or transcript input such as Oliv Notetaker, a CRM connection and a calendar. Email and LinkedIn or Sales Navigator are optional."],[224,"A rep hasn't updated the Core 4 Fields after a meeting."],[227,"A rep shows a pattern that warrants attention, such as consistently missing next-step fields."],[624,"A sales development team books first meetings every day. Each rep reads the research brief between calls and opens with the icebreaker, so no first call starts with \"tell me about your company.\" It's one way to keep AI-assisted prospecting personal."],[102,"A sales development team lets an agent read public LinkedIn profiles and company posts on **Auto Run**. Sending email from Gmail or Outlook stays on **Requires Approval**, so no first touch reaches a prospect unseen. That keeps AI outreach from burning through the target list."],[238,"A sales manager gets the morning brief before the standup and the 1:1 reports every Thursday. Many shorten the daily standup, and some drop it. More on Oliv AI for sales managers and a day in a sales manager's workflow."],[627,"A sales manager opens each Thursday 1:1 with the rep's pipeline, activity and flagged deals already on the page. The conversation starts at strategy instead of status updates."],[127,"A tool is one action an agent is allowed to take, such as finding a record, drafting an email or posting to a channel. Each one is listed on the agent's **Tools** tab with a one-line summary."],[42,"A tool is one action an agent is allowed to take, such as looking up a record, drafting an email or posting to a channel. Every agent in the Oliv AI agent marketplace with a detail page lists its tools on a **Tools** tab. Each tool carries a run mode that decides how much freedom the agent has with it: **Auto Run**, **Requires Approval** or **Agent Decides**."],[509,"About 30 minutes before every meeting linked to an active opportunity in your CRM."],[302,"Account executives"],[551,"Account executives"],[304,"Account managers"],[552,"Account managers"],[432,"After a call"],[480,"After every activity, you get a Slack or preferred-channel message that says it found updates for a number of fields. The **Agent Updates** tab shows each field, its current CRM value, the proposed value and the moment in the conversation behind it. Choose **Accept**, **Edit and accept** or **Reject**."],[369,"After every call, she surfaces proposed CRM updates, such as field values, stage changes and next steps, for the rep to review and approve. Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent handles the execution of those writes."],[418,"Agent builder"],[106,"Agent permissions, from each platform's public documentation:"],[548,"Agent tools"],[1,"Agent tools and run modes"],[655,"Agent tools and run modes: choose which agent actions wait for your approval."],[145,"Agentic sales automation: what changes when software acts, not just suggest